"完整卸载步骤：\n\n            1. 在「设置 → 危险操作」中点击「清理配置信息」，移除 settings.json 中的 Hook 条目和应用数据。\n            2. 退出 CC Peek（菜单栏图标 → 退出）。\n            3. 将 /Applications/CC Peek.app 拖到废纸篓。\n            4. 如已开启开机自启，删除 ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.ccpeek.mac.agent.plist。" = "Full uninstall steps:\n\n            1. Click “Clear configuration data” under Settings → Danger zone to remove the hook entry from settings.json and app data.\n            2. Quit CC Peek (menu bar icon → Quit).\n            3. Drag /Applications/CC Peek.app to the Trash.\n            4. If launch-at-login is on, delete ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.ccpeek.mac.agent.plist.";
"定期检查 ccpeek.com/appcast.xml 是否有新版本" = "Periodically checks ccpeek.com/appcast.xml for new versions";
"实时监控你的 Claude Code 进程状态，\niPhone 放电脑旁边就能随时感知。" = "See your Claude Code session state in real time —\nput your iPhone next to your Mac and a side-glance is enough.";
"实时监控你的 Claude Code 进程状态，\\niPhone 放电脑旁边就能随时感知。" = "See your Claude Code session state in real time —\\nput your iPhone next to your Mac and a side-glance is enough.";
"导出日志" = "Export log";
"将 CC Peek 完全恢复到首次启动状态：清掉 Hook 配置、配对的 iPhone、开机自启、全局快捷键、引导与偏好设置，以及 ~/Library/Application Support/cc-peek/ 下的应用数据。清理后 app 会自动重启。" = "Reset CC Peek to its first-launch state: clear the hook config, paired iPhones, launch-at-login, global shortcut, onboarding state and preferences, and app data under ~/Library/Application Support/cc-peek/. The app will restart automatically afterwards.";
"将清理以下内容:\n            • ~/.claude/settings.json 中的 Hook 条目\n            • 已配对的 iPhone 列表\n            • 开机自启\n            • 全局快捷键设置\n            • 引导与偏好设置 (UserDefaults)\n            • ~/Library/Application Support/cc-peek/ 下的应用数据 (events / 诊断日志 / 归档)\n\n            清理后 CC Peek 会自动重启, 回到首次启动状态. 如需完全卸载, 重启后将 CC Peek.app 从 Applications 拖到废纸篓即可." = "The following will be cleared:\n            • Hook entries in ~/.claude/settings.json\n            • Paired iPhone list\n            • Launch at login\n            • Global shortcut settings\n            • Onboarding state and preferences (UserDefaults)\n            • App data under ~/Library/Application Support/cc-peek/ (events / diagnostic logs / archives)\n\n            CC Peek will restart automatically afterwards, back to its first-launch state. To fully uninstall, drag CC Peek.app from Applications to the Trash after the restart.";
